                                    <h2>Why Home + D&eacute;cor Marketing Is Different From Other D2C</h2>
<p>Home + d&eacute;cor has the longest consideration cycle in D2C. Three economics define everything:</p>
<ul><li><strong>4&ndash;12 week consideration cycle.</strong> Customers save to Pinterest, ask family + friends, sketch room layouts. Retargeting + email lifecycle must sustain interest over weeks.</li><li><strong>Visualisation barrier is real.</strong> Without AR/3D, customers can&rsquo;t imagine the product in their home. Returns + cart abandonment skyrocket. AR/3D drives 1.5&times;&ndash;2.5&times; conversion lift on enabled SKUs.</li><li><strong>High AOV &#8377;5K&ndash;&#8377;50K+ &mdash; EMI/BNPL is essential.</strong> EMI uptake typically 40&ndash;60% on orders &gt;&#8377;15K when displayed prominently on cart + PDP.</li></ul>
<h2>12 Questions to Ask a Home Marketing Agency Before Signing</h2>
<ol><li><strong>How many home + d&eacute;cor brands have you scaled?</strong> Sub-category + revenue stage.</li><li><strong>Do you integrate AR / 3D viewers (Mirrar / Cylindo / Avataar / Threekit)?</strong> If they don&rsquo;t know these, walk away.</li><li><strong>Pinterest marketing experience?</strong> Pinterest drives 35&ndash;55% of category discovery.</li><li><strong>EMI + BNPL integration (Razorpay BNPL + Bajaj Finserv + Simpl + ZestMoney)?</strong> Required for high-AOV.</li><li><strong>WhatsApp design-consult flow build?</strong> Free design-consult booking + designer briefing + product mix recommendation. Drives 18&ndash;28% of revenue for premium brands.</li><li><strong>How do you handle the 4&ndash;12 week consideration cycle?</strong> Email + WhatsApp lifecycle + premium content + retargeting layered.</li><li><strong>How do you handle high shipping + return logistics costs?</strong> Pre-purchase confidence-building reduces returns 20&ndash;35%.</li><li><strong>Multi-room / multi-style customer segments?</strong> Different journeys for different buyer types.</li><li><strong>Reporting cadence?</strong> Weekly blended ROAS + AOV + AR-engagement metrics.</li><li><strong>Contract structure?</strong> Fixed retainer + spend pass-through.</li><li><strong>Account + AR / 3D + email + WhatsApp ownership?</strong> Yours.</li><li><strong>What do you say no to?</strong></li></ol>
<h2>4 Honest Red Flags When Hiring a Home Marketing Agency</h2>
<ol><li><strong>No AR / 3D viewer integration.</strong> Visualisation barrier is the #1 home D2C blocker. Agencies without AR experience leave 50&ndash;100% conversion lift on the table.</li><li><strong>Pinterest treated as &ldquo;optional&rdquo;.</strong> Pinterest is 35&ndash;55% of category discovery. Agencies that don&rsquo;t do Pinterest aren&rsquo;t doing home properly.</li><li><strong>No EMI/BNPL strategy.</strong> EMI uptake 40&ndash;60% on &gt;&#8377;15K orders. Without prominent EMI display, you lose half the conversion.</li><li><strong>No design-consult / WhatsApp concierge play.</strong> Premium home brands need consult-led conversion for &#8377;25K+ orders.</li></ol>
